      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary reserve and functional state of myocardium were studied in 27 patients with unstable angina and myocardial infarction which had developed in spite of the treatment. Non-invasive study included stress-tests (transesophageal electrocardiostimulation, bicycle ergometry [correction of veloergometry)], echocardiography and Holter's monitoring. Possibility of early forming of risk group with consequent optimization of the treatment was shown."},
